description:
Edit repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/advertised-shape-coverage-scan.ts. TWO string replacements in that ONE file. Change nothing else.

An empty-string env var defeats the `??` default. This container exports some endpoint variables as EMPTY STRINGS, and `??` falls back only on null/undefined — never on "". So `process.env["DISCOVERY_VESSEL_ENDPOINT"] ?? "http://127.0.0.1:8100"` yields "" and the fetch below is issued against an empty endpoint instead of the intended default. The repo already has the fix helper: `env(key, fallback)` in src/config.ts treats an empty/whitespace-only value as absent.

EDIT 1 — replace this exact existing line:

import type { ResolverResult } from "./types.js";

with:

import type { ResolverResult } from "./types.js";
import { env } from "../config.js";

EDIT 2 — replace this exact existing line:

    const endpoint = process.env["DISCOVERY_VESSEL_ENDPOINT"] ?? "http://127.0.0.1:8100";

with:

    const endpoint = env("DISCOVERY_VESSEL_ENDPOINT", "http://127.0.0.1:8100");

Do not change the METABOB_API_KEY line beneath it: an API key is not an endpoint, and an empty key is a legitimate "no credential".

The change must typecheck (bun run lint). VERIFY BY CONSEQUENCE: with DISCOVERY_VESSEL_ENDPOINT exported as the empty string, `endpoint` is "http://127.0.0.1:8100" rather than "", so the request goes to the discovery vessel instead of to a relative path.

